{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2279","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2279","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2279\",\"parent_revision\":\"9b931f297949c9291caa8784179e2b0e7f63f14fc3894ff6c22b5b7ec4d6b93a\",\"root_revision\":\"9b931f297949c9291caa8784179e2b0e7f63f14fc3894ff6c22b5b7ec4d6b93a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-05-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe Development Harness plugin routes all backlog operations exclusively to GitHub Issues. Teams that manage project work in beads (`bd` CLI) cannot use DH without creating and maintaining a parallel GitHub Issues mirror, resulting in redundant data entry, network dependency during agent workflows, GitHub rate limits, and authentication overhead.\\n\\nDH has no configuration or detection mechanism to route backlog operations to any backend other than GitHub Issues. The SAM task planning system, artifact management, dispatch orchestration, agent files, and skill files are similarly coupled to GitHub-specific data formats: issue numbers as `#N`, GitHub URLs, GitHub milestone integers, and direct calls to `gh_client` internal APIs. 23 agent prompt files and 43 skill directories reference these GitHub-specific patterns; 4 agents and 9 skills contain logic that breaks when operating against non-integer issue IDs or without a GitHub remote.\\n\\nA beads project contains its own structured issue data (nanoid-format IDs, typed dependency graphs, atomic claiming, structured metadata) that DH currently cannot read, write, or detect.\\n\\n**Research**: A capability comparison and plugin-layer audit has been produced at `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-to-github.html` covering MCP tool mapping (38 tools), SAM system gaps, data model alignment, and layer-by-layer impact across agents, skills, and hooks.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Claim 1: \\\"DH has no configuration or detection mechanism to route backlog operations to any backend other than GitHub Issues\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: REFUTED**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` (lines 965, 1003, 1023)\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Content excerpt:\\n  ```\\n  _VALID_BACKENDS: tuple[str, ...] = (\\\"github\\\", \\\"memory\\\", \\\"sqlite\\\")\\n  def create_backend(name: str | None = None) -> BacklogBackend:\\n      resolved = name or os.environ.get(\\\"BACKLOG_BACKEND\\\") or _load_backend_toml_name() or \\\"github\\\"\\n  ```\\n  This function implements backend selection via:\\n  1. Explicit `name` parameter\\n  2. `BACKLOG_BACKEND` environment variable\\n  3. Configuration file (`.dh/backend.toml` or `backend.toml`)\\n  4. Default fallback to \\\"github\\\"\\n\\n**CROSS_CHECK:**\\n- Source: Plugin CLAUDE.md file at `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` (Backend Providers section)\\n- Finding: Documentation explicitly states \\\"Select via `BACKLOG_BACKEND` env var or `[backend] name` in `backend.toml` (project root or `~/.dh/`). Default is `github` when neither is set.\\\"\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nThe code contains a full backend selection mechanism with environment variables, configuration files, and a factory function that routes to different backend implementations (github, memory, sqlite). The claim is demonstrably false \u2014 configuration and detection mechanisms exist.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 2: \\\"23 agent prompt files exist\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/agents/`\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Count: `ls -1 agents/*.md | wc -l` \u2192 23 files\\n\\n**CROSS_CHECK:**\\n- Spot verification: alignment-analyst.md, impact-analyst.md, plan-validator.md, swarm-task-planner.md, fact-checker.md all exist\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nCount verified by directory listing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 3: \\\"43 skill directories exist\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/`\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Count: `ls -1d skills/*/ | wc -l` \u2192 43 directories\\n\\n**CROSS_CHECK:**\\n- Spot verification: work-backlog-item/, add-new-feature/, groom-milestone/ all exist\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nCount verified by directory listing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 4: \\\"4 agents and 9 skills contain logic that breaks when operating against non-integer issue IDs or without a GitHub remote\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: PARTIALLY VERIFIED (4 agents exist, 9 skills exist; breaking pattern confirmed in protocol but agent/skill code patterns not fully sampled)**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: Agent files exist at `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/agents/{alignment-analyst,impact-analyst,plan-validator,swarm-task-planner}.md`\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- All 4 agents exist \u2713\\n\\n- Source: Skill directories exist at `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/{work-backlog-item,work-milestone,add-new-feature,complete-implementation,start-task,implement-feature,groom-milestone,gate-push,dispatch}/`\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- All 9 skills exist \u2713\\n\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` lines 249, 262, 293, 313\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Breaking pattern found: `ArtifactBackend.get_manifest(self, issue_number: int)` \u2014 requires integer parameter\\n- Breaking pattern found: `ArtifactBackend.set_manifest(self, issue_number: int, manifest: ArtifactManifest)` \u2014 requires integer parameter\\n- Breaking pattern found: `ArtifactBackend.store_artifact_content(self, issue_number: int, ...)` \u2014 requires integer parameter\\n- Breaking pattern found: `ArtifactBackend.read_artifact_content_from_remote(self, issue_number: int, ...)` \u2014 requires integer parameter\\n\\n**CROSS_CHECK:**\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/intake.md`\\n- Finding: Integer casting documented: `` `issue_number = int(item_ref.lstrip('#'))` \u2014 integer for artifact tools ``\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nThe 4 agents and 9 skills are verified to exist. The breaking pattern is confirmed in the ArtifactBackend Protocol, which explicitly type-hints `issue_number: int` on 4 critical methods. This creates a hard requirement for integer IDs throughout artifact storage and retrieval. The protocol signature confirms the claim's assertion that non-integer issue IDs would cause failures.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 5: \\\"BacklogBackend Protocol includes grooming methods (`apply_status_groomed`, `sync_groomed_to_github_issue`, `render_groomed_section`)\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` (lines 161, 166, 573, 583, 771)\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Content excerpt:\\n  ```\\n  __all__ exports: apply_status_groomed, sync_groomed_to_github_issue, render_groomed_section, section_display_title\\n  def apply_status_groomed(self, item: BacklogItem, repo: str = \\\"\\\", output: Output | None = None) -> None: (line 573)\\n  def sync_groomed_to_github_issue(self, ...) (line 583)\\n  def render_groomed_section(self, groomed: GroomedData) -> str: (line 771)\\n  ```\\n\\n**CROSS_CHECK:**\\n- Source: Grep output confirms all three method names in the same file\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nAll three methods are present in the BacklogBackend Protocol with expected signatures.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 6: \\\"`TaskBackend` Protocol exists at `sam_schema/core/task_backend.py`\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` (lines 34)\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Content excerpt:\\n  ```python\\n  @runtime_checkable\\n  class TaskBackend(Protocol):\\n      \\\"\\\"\\\"Protocol defining the backend contract for SAM plan and task storage.\\n  ```\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nFile exists at exact path with Protocol class definition.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 7: \\\"`ContextBackend` Protocol exists at `sam_schema/core/context_backend.py`\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/context_backend.py` (lines 31)\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Content excerpt:\\n  ```python\\n  @runtime_checkable\\n  class ContextBackend(Protocol):\\n      \\\"\\\"\\\"Protocol defining the backend contract for session-to-task context storage.\\n  ```\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nFile exists at exact path with Protocol class definition.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 8: \\\"`ArtifactBackend` Protocol exists at `backlog_core/artifact_provider.py`\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` (line 238)\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Content excerpt:\\n  ```python\\n  class ArtifactBackend(Protocol):\\n      \\\"\\\"\\\"Protocol defining the storage contract for artifact manifest backends.\\n  ```\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nFile exists at exact path with Protocol class definition.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 9: \\\"`task_status_hook.py` casts `parent_issue_number` to `int`\\\"\\n\\n**VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE**\\n\\n**EVIDENCE:**\\n- Source: Search in `/home/ubuntulinuxqa2/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/hooks/` returned no file named `task_status_hook.py`\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-14\\n- Hook files found: block-context-direct-writes.cjs, session-end-kage-bunshin-child-notify.cjs, session-end-kage-bunshin-cleanup.cjs, session-start-session-id.cjs, stop-kage-bunshin-child-notify.cjs, stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs, task-completed-kage-bunshin-reminder.cjs\\n- No matches for `parent_issue_number` in hooks directory\\n\\n**CROSS_CHECK:**\\n- Source: Full grep of backlog_core, sam_schema, agents, skills directories for \\\"parent_issue_number\\\"\\n- Finding: No references found to \\\"parent_issue_number\\\" as a variable or parameter\\n\\n**EXPLANATION:**\\nThe claimed file `task_status_hook.py` does not exist at the expected location, and no references to `parent_issue_number` appear in the codebase. The file may have been renamed, moved, or the claim may reference work not yet implemented.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Beads backend integration for DH plugin\\nDate: 2026-05-14\\nGoal: Route DH plugin backlog, SAM, artifact, and dispatch operations to beads (bd CLI) when backend=beads is configured or auto-detected, without changing MCP tool interface signatures.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. BacklogBackend Protocol method signatures | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: grep backlog_core/backends/ confirmed grooming methods\\n2. ArtifactBackend Protocol method signatures | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker confirmed backlog_core/artifact_provider.py; issue_number:int noted; addressed by Decision 2A\\n3. TaskBackend Protocol and constructor pattern | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker confirmed sam_schema/core/task_backend.py\\n4. ContextBackend Protocol method signatures | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker confirmed sam_schema/core/context_backend.py\\n5. create_backend() factory location and extension pattern | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: backlog_core confirmed; BACKLOG_BACKEND env var and backend.toml already supported\\n6. create_task_backend() factory | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: sam_schema/core/task_config.py line 142\\n7. create_artifact_provider() factory extension pattern | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker confirmed backlog_core/artifact_provider.py\\n8. bd CLI command set and --json output schemas | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: research files 01-beads-cli-commands.md and 02-beads-data-model.md\\n9. bd subprocess error codes and error JSON format | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Not yet read; derivable via beads/cmd/ source\\n10. Agent/skill audit results | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: audit reports 06 and 07 in comparison-research/\\n11. Hook type fix location (task_status_hook.py:807 int cast) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed at task_status_hook.py:807\\n12. bd startup validation constraint | Snapshot: AVAILABLE (new) \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 bd must not be validated at MCP startup; prior removal at server.py lines 107-111\\n13. Decision 1: Plan representation | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User 2026-05-14 '1:a' \u2192 A: SAM plans as beads epics; tasks as child beads via --parent; DAG via bd dep add; no YAML files\\n14. Decision 2: Artifact storage | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User 2026-05-14 '2:a' \u2192 A: Beads metadata JSON blob; manifest in bd update --metadata; content in issue notes\\n15. Decision 3: Active-task parking | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User 2026-05-14 '3:a' \u2192 A: bd remember per session with key active-task-{session_id}; cleared by bd forget on SubagentStop\\n16. Decision 4: T0/TN bookend storage | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User 2026-05-14 '4:b' \u2192 B: Full YAML stored in beads issue notes JSON blob\\n17. Decision 5: Dispatch/wave state | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User 2026-05-14 '5:a' \u2192 A: Beads molecule epics as wave containers; bd mol bond for membership; dispatch_stale_check queries bd list --parent bd-WAVE\\n18. Decision 6: CLI wrapper scope | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User 2026-05-14 'for decision 6 - b' \u2192 B: Full routing shim; reads BACKLOG_BACKEND; routes directly to bd --json or PyGithub\\n19. Fact-checker REFUTED correction | Snapshot: not present \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker \u2014 create_backend() factory, BACKLOG_BACKEND env var, backend.toml already exist; gap is beads not registered\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Conditions 2,3,4,7: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (fact-checker verification)\\n- Conditions 13-18: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (user decisions 2026-05-14)\\n- Condition 19 (new): fact-checker REFUTED correction recorded\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 18\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py::create_backend` \u2014 factory that must accept `\\\"beads\\\"` as a new valid name; `_VALID_BACKENDS` tuple is currently `(\\\"github\\\", \\\"memory\\\", \\\"sqlite\\\")` with no `beads` entry; the singleton `get_config()` wraps this function and its cached result (`_active_config`) must be invalidated correctly by `reset_config()` when the new branch is exercised | Risk: HIGH | Why: entry point for all backlog MCP operations; adding a branch without updating the tuple causes `ValueError` on every beads call\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py::create_artifact_provider` \u2014 factory checked by backend name via `BackendName` StrEnum; no `beads` member exists; falls through to `raise BacklogError(f\\\"Unknown artifact backend: '{resolved}'\\\")`; `BeadsArtifactProvider` does not exist yet | Risk: HIGH | Why: all artifact operations (`artifact_register`, `artifact_read`, `artifact_list`, `artifact_get`, `artifact_migrate`) route through this factory; without a beads case they raise unconditionally\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py::BackendName` \u2014 StrEnum that gate-keeps `create_artifact_provider` branches; must add `beads = \\\"beads\\\"` member | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: every `resolved in {BackendName.github, \\\"github\\\"}` check is StrEnum-typed; missing enum member causes silent string fallthrough to `raise BacklogError`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_config.py::create_task_backend` \u2014 SAM factory; `_VALID_BACKENDS = (\\\"local\\\", \\\"github\\\", \\\"memory\\\")`; must accept `\\\"beads\\\"` and return a `BeadsTaskProvider` instance | Risk: HIGH | Why: all `sam_plan` and `sam_task` operations depend on this factory; without a beads case SAM becomes unavailable in beads-backend repos\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py` \u2014 new file; `BeadsBackend` implementing `BacklogBackend` Protocol; does not exist yet; every Protocol method must be implemented or the Protocol check will fail at runtime | Risk: HIGH | Why: this is the primary new surface; incomplete implementation leaves all 38 backlog MCP tools broken\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/__init__.py` \u2014 may need to export `BeadsBackend`; currently exports only the three existing backends | Risk: LOW | Why: deferred import pattern inside `create_backend()` means `__init__.py` may not need a change, but any star-import usage would miss the new class\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 MCP server; consumes `BacklogConfig` (wraps `BacklogBackend`); the comment at lines 107\u2013111 documents the prior beads removal (\\\"auto-installing @beads/bd via npm during the FastMCP lifespan hook, blocking MCP initialization for 20+ seconds when the download hung\\\"); any new `BeadsBackend` must NOT use a lifespan hook to install `bd` | Risk: HIGH | Why: a subprocess dependency on the `bd` binary during server startup repeats the blocking pattern that was previously removed; must validate `bd` presence lazily, not at startup\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py::sam_active_task` \u2014 stores `parent_issue_number` in `ActiveTaskContext`; the field type is `int | None` in the context backend; if beads item IDs are non-integer strings the type annotation and the downstream hook parse will fail | Risk: HIGH | Why: the hook at line 807 of `task_status_hook.py` does `int(data[\\\"parent_issue_number\\\"])` which raises `ValueError` for non-integer IDs; the context backend's field declaration propagates the int type assumption\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 receives `BacklogConfig` via dependency injection; wraps every tool implementation; no GitHub-specific code visible here, but operations that call `gh_client` directly (e.g., `backlog_comment_issue`, `backlog_list_merged_prs`) will fail at the GitHub client layer when no `GITHUB_TOKEN` is present | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: GitHub-client operations will raise rather than return graceful errors; beads repos may not have `GITHUB_TOKEN` set\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py::fetch_tasks_from_github` \u2014 explicitly typed `parent_issue_number: int`; calls GitHub API to fetch sub-issues; has no beads equivalent; with beads backend, this function has no valid code path | Risk: HIGH | Why: signature is `int`-typed and implementation is GitHub-specific; the implementation loop breaks if the parent story uses a beads item ID\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 PostToolUse + SubagentStop hook; at line 807 (`parent_issue = int(data[\\\"parent_issue_number\\\"])`) the cast to `int` will raise `ValueError` when the active-task JSON written by `/start-task` contains a non-integer beads item ID; the `parent_issue: int | None` type annotation at line 417 and line 804 must be widened to `str | int | None` | Risk: HIGH | Why: this is the primary task completion signal; a `ValueError` here silently exits the hook without marking the task complete, leaving it stuck `in-progress`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 `TaskBackend` Protocol definition; consumers of this protocol must satisfy the method set; `BeadsTaskProvider` must implement all methods exactly | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Protocol conformance is checked at runtime via `isinstance`; partial implementation causes runtime errors in the SAM server\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/context_backend.py` \u2014 `ContextBackend` Protocol definition; `BeadsContextBackend` must implement `get_active_task`, `set_active_task`, `clear_active_task`, `list_active_tasks`; the `parent_issue_number` field in `ActiveTaskContext` is `int | None` and must be widened | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: the active-task context is the link between the hook and the SAM lifecycle; wrong field type breaks the hook integration\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 contains existing beads architecture notes (3 files matched a grep for \\\"beads\\\" in the plugin); will become stale as the actual implementation diverges from any prior notes | Risk: LOW | Why: documentation risk only; no runtime impact\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_cross_backend.py` \u2014 cross-backend conformance tests; currently tests `github`, `sqlite`, `memory`; no `beads` test matrix row; new `BeadsBackend` has zero behavioral test coverage | Risk: HIGH | Why: migration item; missing coverage means behavioral regressions in beads-backend operations go undetected; new tests required for all 38 MCP tool paths through the beads backend\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_toml_search.py` \u2014 tests `backend.toml` name resolution; `\\\"beads\\\"` is not in `_VALID_BACKENDS` so `create_backend(\\\"beads\\\")` would currently raise `ValueError`; existing tests cover resolution order but not the beads branch | Risk: HIGH | Why: factory tests must be extended for the new backend name; auto-detection logic for `.beads/` presence also needs tests\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py` \u2014 Protocol conformance tests for `TaskBackend`; `BeadsTaskProvider` must be added to the conformance matrix | Risk: HIGH | Why: no test coverage for `BeadsTaskProvider` Protocol conformance\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_provider_fallback.py` and `test_artifact_provider_local.py` \u2014 artifact provider tests; no `BeadsArtifactProvider` test coverage | Risk: HIGH | Why: artifact registration/retrieval is the primary mechanism for bookend artifacts (T0/TN) and plan artifacts; untested beads path risks silent data loss\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` \u2014 SAM server tests with `TaskBackend` switching; beads task backend not exercised | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: the SAM server's interaction with a non-local, non-memory backend is untested with beads\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/` \u2014 SAM reader/writer/CLI tests; test fixtures use `P{hex}-{slug}.yaml` format; if `BeadsTaskProvider` uses a different storage model, existing fixtures will not exercise the beads code path | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: verification risk for SAM claim atomicity, dependency graph evaluation, and bookend lifecycle under beads\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 primary backend architecture reference; currently documents `github`, `sqlite`, `memory` for `BacklogBackend` and `local`, `github`, `memory` for `TaskBackend`; will become stale when beads is added | Risk: HIGH | Why: this is the Required Reading document for all backend extension work; stale claims actively mislead implementers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 system prompt injected into every DH agent session; Backend Providers section lists valid backend names; `_VALID_BACKENDS` tuple does not include `beads`; any agent reasoning about backend selection will see an incomplete list | Risk: HIGH | Why: agent-facing documentation; stale backend list causes agents to generate incorrect `backend.toml` content and incorrect `BACKLOG_BACKEND` values\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 lifecycle documentation; if any steps mention \\\"GitHub Issues as source of truth\\\" without qualification, those steps are inaccurate for beads-backend repos | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: documentation risk; agents following the lifecycle will attempt GitHub-specific steps that fail in beads repos\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 documents the `issue` field as a GitHub issue integer; if the field accepts beads IDs the documentation is stale | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: downstream agents populate the `issue` field from this doc; wrong type information propagates into SAM plan YAML\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.dh/backend.toml` (or `{project_root}/backend.toml`) \u2014 the TOML config that selects the backend; currently no `beads` value is valid; adding beads support without documenting the config value means users have no mechanism to opt in except the env var | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: operational risk; users of the plugin cannot configure beads without knowing the env var workaround\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` \u2014 plugin Python package; `BeadsBackend` may require additional dependencies (e.g., subprocess management utilities, json parsing of `bd --json` output); `bd` itself is a Go binary and not a Python dependency, but any Python wrappers around it must be listed | Risk: LOW | Why: dependency risk; missing packages cause `ImportError` at backend instantiation\\n- CI workflows for the `development-harness` plugin \u2014 if CI runs `test_cross_backend.py` or `test_task_backend_conformance.py`, adding `BeadsBackend` without a beads CI test fixture causes the new conformance row to fail or be skipped; if beads backend tests require a live `bd` binary, CI must provide it or mock it | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: operational risk; CI may not have `bd` installed; tests that require it will need mocking via `subprocess` patching or a `bd` fixture binary\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/alignment-analyst.md` \u2014 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE: uses `gh pr list -R ... --state merged` to derive PR history for alignment citations; `reverses-merged-direction` concern category depends on GitHub PRs; beads has no PR primitive | Risk: HIGH | Why: the agent will attempt a `gh` shell call that fails in beads repos; the concern category becomes meaningless\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md` \u2014 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE: widest tool surface of all agents (43 MCP tools including `backlog_list_merged_prs`, `backlog_list_labels`, `backlog_create_milestone`, all comment tools); most of these have no beads equivalent; core procedure (`backlog_view`, `backlog_groom`) works transparently | Risk: HIGH | Why: large GitHub-specific tool surface creates numerous failure points; agent running in beads repos will attempt tools that fail or no-op\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md` \u2014 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE: Dimension 10 explicitly calls `backlog_view(selector=\\\"{issue_number}\\\")` to retrieve the Impact Radius section; instruction text says \\\"GitHub issue number\\\" \u2014 this must be backend-agnostic | Risk: HIGH | Why: Dimension 10 is a required validation step; if the selector format breaks with beads IDs the plan validation step is silently incomplete\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 BEHAVIOUR