ns/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE: `backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks(parent_issue_number=N)` uses GitHub issue integer as primary key; `from #{issue}` attribution in groom calls; `artifact_register` at bookend setup passes integer `issue_number` | Risk: HIGH | Why: the implement-feature loop is the primary execution driver; integer-typed parent issue number will fail with beads string IDs\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` \u2014 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE: references `backlog_core.gh_client.update_task_status(repo, github_issue, \\\"in-progress\\\")` \u2014 a GitHub-specific internal API call; must route through backend-agnostic `backlog_update` instead | Risk: HIGH | Why: task start syncs status to GitHub sub-issues; this path does not exist in beads and will silently fail or raise\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE: deepest GitHub entanglement; accepts `#N` and GitHub URLs as input; states \\\"Primary source of truth is GitHub Issues\\\"; has `setup-github` mode to initialize labels, project, and milestone | Risk: HIGH | Why: the skill's identity is GitHub-coupled; beads repos need a `setup-beads` mode and a different source-of-truth statement\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE: calls `github_branches create/merge/delete`; creates integration branch at `milestone/{N}-{slug}` embedding the GitHub milestone number; milestone number N is a GitHub milestone integer | Risk: HIGH | Why: `github_branches` is a GitHub-specific tool; the integration branch naming convention must be adapted for beads repos\\n- 19 additional agents and skills with INSTRUCTION_UPDATE classification (overuse of GitHub-specific tools in frontmatter `tools:` lists; `issue_number` terminology in procedure steps mapping to bead IDs; `sync`/`pull`/`normalize` MCP tools unavailable with beads): `backlog-item-groomer`, `classifier`,