ask_status()` | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE; deepest GitHub entanglement; `setup-github` mode | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE; `github_branches` MCP tool; milestone number as branch name | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: lifecycle steps mention GitHub as source of truth | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: `issue` field documented as GitHub integer | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- 19 agent/skill files with INSTRUCTION_UPDATE classification | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: frontmatter over-broad tool lists; `issue_number` terminology; GitHub sync tools unavailable; see `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/06-agents-beads-integration.md` and `07-skills-hooks-beads-integration.md` | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` \u2014 factory gate for all 38 backlog MCP tools; no beads branch exists; adding it incorrectly leaves all tools broken\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 primary task completion signal; `int()` cast at line 807 will raise on non-integer beads IDs and silently leave tasks stuck `in-progress`\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 the prior beads integration was removed because a lifespan hook blocked MCP initialization for 20+ seconds; any new integration must validate `bd` lazily, not at startup\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 generates task YAML with integer `issue:` field that propagates downstream into 6+ other agents; wrong type assumption infects every bookend artifact registration\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 deepest GitHub entanglement; entire lifecycle model (labels = status) has no beads equivalent\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - compatibility: `issue_number: int` assumption in `artifact_register`, `sam_active_task`, `sam_plan(issue=N)`, and `implementation_manager.py` signature; beads IDs are non-integer\\n  - migration: 5 MCP tool groups have no beads equivalent (PR listing, labels, GitHub Projects, issue comments, GitHub-only sync); 4 agent/skill workflows use GitHub-specific primitives that must be replaced\\n  - behavioral: `task_status_hook.py` silent failure on `ValueError` leaves tasks stuck; `gate-push` shell script silently produces wrong repo slug\\n  - verification: zero test coverage for `BeadsBackend`, `BeadsTaskProvider`, `BeadsArtifactProvider` conformance; claim atomicity and dependency graph correctness unverified for beads\\n  - operational: prior `bd` auto-install blocked MCP startup; subprocess dependency on `bd` binary must be validated lazily\\n  - scope: this change touches 38 MCP tools, 6 factory functions, 3 Protocol files, 2 hook files, 12 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE agents/skills, 19 INSTRUCTION_UPDATE agents/skills, and 5 documentation files \u2014 larger than the item description's single \\\"add BeadsBackend\\\" framing\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - 6 open architectural decisions documented in the RT-ICA section are unresolved: plan representation in beads, artifact storage mechanism, active-task parking without GitHub, bookend result storage, dispatch/wave state with beads, CLI wrapper vs in-process routing. Each MISSING decision is a blocking gap for the corresponding implementation task.\\n  - `implementation_manager.py::fetch_tasks_from_github` is a GitHub-specific function that must be reimplemented as `fetch_tasks_from_beads`; this was not in the original scope description.\\n  - The `BackendName` StrEnum in `artifact_provider.py` must be extended alongside the factory \u2014 this is a second point of change not mentioned in the item summary.\\n  - The prior beads removal comment in `server.py` (lines 107\u2013111) establishes a hard constraint: `bd` must not be auto-installed at MCP startup. This constraint must be carried into the implementation design for `BeadsBackend.__init__`.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible (`backend_protocol.py`, `artifact_provider.py`, `task_config.py`, `beads_backend.py` \u2014 new file, `context_backend.py`)\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible (`server.py` startup constraint, `sam_schema/server.py` `parent_issue_number` type, `task_status_hook.py` line 807 cast, `implementation_manager.py` GitHub-only function)\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added (cross-backend, backend-toml, task-backend-conformance, artifact-provider tests all need beads rows)\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated (`backend-providers.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `backlog-item-lifecycle.md`, `TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md`)\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated (`backend.toml` documentation; CI `bd` binary availability for tests)\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated (12 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE + 19 INSTRUCTION_UPDATE items; full list in `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/06-agents-beads-integration.md` and `07-skills-hooks-beads-integration.md`)\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (5 MISSING + 5 PARTIAL capabilities in the migration matrix above require explicit design decisions before implementation)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (`BackendName` StrEnum, `implementation_manager.py` GitHub-typed function, prior `bd` auto-install removal constraint in `server.py` lines 107-111)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Alignment assessment:** ALIGNED (with architectural constraints)\\n\\n### Mission Fit\\n\\nThe proposed beads backend integration aligns with the development-harness plugin's core mission and design principles:\\n\\n1. **Language-agnostic backend abstraction is core to the harness identity** \u2014 CLAUDE.md line 1 states the plugin is \\\"language-agnostic.\\\" The Composition Model section (lines 174\u2013187) explicitly separates \\\"what the harness owns\\\" (process, touchpoints, artifact management) from \\\"what plugins own\\\" (specialists, gates). Backend abstraction follows this same separation: the harness owns the process flow; the backend owns the storage primitive.\\n\\n2. **Protocol-based backend pattern is an established, merged architectural direction** \u2014 Three backends already implement the `BacklogBackend` Protocol (GitHub, SQLite, InMemory; PR #413 merged 2026-03-03, PR #387 merged 2026-03-02). The `ArtifactBackend` Protocol is fully documented (PR #1482 merged 2026-04-29). Adding a fourth backend (beads) follows the exact same pattern as these predecessors.\\n\\n3. **Backend selection mechanism preserves MCP tool interface stability** \u2014 The proposal's constraint \\\"without changing MCP tool interface signatures\\\" aligns with the design principle: \\\"Every stage produces an MCP-registered artifact... stored via `artifact_register` and retrieved via `artifact_read`, never via direct filesystem paths\\\" (CLAUDE.md line 16). New backends implement the same Protocol signatures; consumers call the same MCP tools regardless of backend.\\n\\n4. **Factory extension pattern is established and documented** \u2014 The `create_backend()` factory (backend_protocol.py lines 965\u20131023) implements resolution order: explicit name parameter \u2192 `BACKLOG_BACKEND` env var \u2192 `backend.toml` \u2192 default. This pattern mirrors the existing `create_task_backend()` (task_config.py) and `create_artifact_provider()` (artifact_provider.py) factories. Beads integration follows the same precedent.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| violates-design-principle | Subprocess validation of `bd` binary must occur at backend instantiation (implied by implementation approach) | Prior beads removal established hard constraint: \\\"auto-installing @beads/bd via npm during the FastMCP lifespan hook, blocking MCP initialization for 20+ seconds when the download hung\\\" | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` lines 107\u2013111 |\\n| expands-scope-beyond-mission | Item description frames work as \\\"add BeadsBackend\\\" but actual scope includes: (1) type widening `parent_issue_number: int \u2192 str \\\\| int \\\\| None`, (2) hook file updates at `task_status_hook.py` line 807, (3) agent/skill instruction changes (12 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE + 19 INSTRUCTION_UPDATE items), (4) 6 architectural decision resolutions not yet made | Harness owns process and artifact management, not individual system-wide type propagation; scope creep beyond backend implementation indicates design boundaries not yet established | Impact Radius \\\"Systems Inventory\\\" section enumerates 23 files requiring changes; RT-ICA section lists 6 unresolved architectural decisions blocking implementation |\\n| reverses-merged-direction | Integration approach must decide: (a) shell out to `bd` CLI for every operation (subprocess calls with JSON parsing), (b) use beads Go library via Python FFI, (c) hybrid \u2014 was not decided in this item | PR #1773 (2026-04-14) added `append_task` and `finalize` for incremental plan building, establishing single-writer assumption for plan append. CLI wrapper vs in-process routing decision affects whether this assumption holds for BeadsTaskProvider | PR #1773 commit message and `append_task` docstring in `sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` establish atomicity expectations |\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n**3 concerns identified:**\\n\\n- 1 violates-design-principle (startup validation constraint from prior beads removal)\\n- 1 expands-scope-beyond-mission (scope creep: type widening, hook updates, agent/skill changes beyond the stated \\\"add BeadsBackend\\\" frame)\\n- 1 reverses-merged-direction (CLI vs FFI routing decision not addressed; affects atomicity contract from #1773)\\n\\n**Verdict rationale:**\\n\\nThe proposed beads backend integration is conceptually ALIGNED with the plugin's mission and design principles. The Protocol-based backend pattern, factory extension pattern, and MCP tool interface stability are all established architectural directions. However, implementation success depends on:\\n\\n1. **Resolving the startup validation constraint:** The `bd` binary must be validated lazily (at first use), not at MCP initialization, per the hard constraint from the prior beads removal (server.py lines 107\u2013111). This constraint must be designed into `BeadsBackend.__init__` or a lazy validation wrapper.\\n\\n2. **Narrowing scope before task decomposition:** Six architectural decisions listed in the RT-ICA section (plan representation, artifact storage, active-task parking, bookend storage, dispatch state, CLI routing) must be resolved before task writing begins. The type widening (`parent_issue_number: int \u2192 str | int | None`) that cascades into 23 files requires a clear design boundary to avoid scope creep.\\n\\n3. **Documenting the CLI wrapper decision:** The choice between subprocess, FFI, or hybrid approach affects the single-writer assumption for plan append (established in PR #1773). This decision must be documented before `BeadsTaskProvider` implementation.\\n\\nAll three concerns are addressable through design phase work, not code-level fixes. The alignment is fundamentally sound; the blockers are architectural, not directional.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **beads backend integration for dh plugin** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Design research session \u2014 docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-to-github.html (2026-05-14)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-14\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:bf42ee8d4576f5d3267dd138bfc4079e -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-14)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 this is a feature item, not a defect. No steps to reproduce a failure exist; the absence of beads backend support is the gap.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n9/10 \u2014 Teams using `bd` as their project management backend currently cannot use DH workflows at all without maintaining a parallel GitHub Issues mirror. The integration removes a complete class of users from DH's reachable audience and creates redundant work for those who adopt both tools. All 6 architectural decisions are now resolved (RT-ICA: APPROVED, all 19 conditions AVAILABLE), unblocking planning.\\n\\nEffort: XL \u2014 The impact radius spans 6 producer files (including one new file), 4 consumer files with breaking type incompatibilities, 5 test file groups with zero beads coverage, 5 documentation files, 12 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE agent/skill files, and 19 INSTRUCTION_UPDATE agent/skill files. Six separate capability layers must be completed (backend registration, backlog CRUD, SAM task management, artifact storage, dispatch/wave state, agent and skill instruction sweep) before end-to-end beads workflows are functional. The `task_status_hook.py:807` int cast and `parent_issue_number: int` type widening cascade through multiple files across both backlog and SAM subsystems.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**Who is affected:**\\n- Teams using `bd` (beads CLI) for project management who want DH agent workflows without a GitHub remote\\n- DH plugin users who hit GitHub rate limits or have no GitHub authentication during agent sessions\\n- Agents using DH skills in repositories where the git remote is not GitHub\\n\\n**What workflows change:**\\n- All 38 backlog MCP tools currently route exclusively to GitHub Issues; with beads backend they route through `BeadsBackend` when `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads` is set or auto-detected via `.beads/` directory\\n- SAM task planning (`sam_plan`, `sam_task`) currently stores plan YAML on disk; with beads backend, SAM plans map to beads epics and tasks map to child beads via `--parent`, with no YAML plan files on disk\\n- Active-task parking currently uses context backend storage; with beads backend it uses `bd remember` per session (key `active-task-{session_id}`) and `bd forget` on SubagentStop\\n- Dispatch/wave state currently uses SQLite; with beads backend it uses beads molecule epics as wave containers with `bd mol bond` for membership\\n\\n**What becomes unavailable during transition (capabilities without beads equivalents):**\\n- Pull request listing (`backlog_list_merged_prs`) \u2014 no beads PR primitive\\n- Label management (`backlog_list_labels`) \u2014 beads has no label concept\\n- GitHub Projects V2 (`backlog_create_project`, `backlog_list_projects`) \u2014 no beads equivalent\\n- Issue comments (`backlog_comment_issue`, `backlog_list_comments`, `backlog_read_comment`) \u2014 no beads equivalent\\n- GitHub-only sync operations (`backlog_sync`, `backlog_pull`, `backlog_normalize`) \u2014 not applicable when beads is the source of truth\\n- `verified=True` status label (`backlog_update(verified=True)`) \u2014 no label system in beads\\n\\n**Type compatibility break (currently broken for any beads ID):**\\n- `task_status_hook.py:807` does `int(data[\\\"parent_issue_number\\\"])` \u2014 raises `ValueError` for non-integer beads IDs, silently leaving tasks stuck `in-progress`\\n- `ArtifactBackend` Protocol methods type `issue_number: int` \u2014 4 methods reject non-integer IDs at the type level\\n- `implementation_manager.py::fetch_tasks_from_github(parent_issue_number: int)` \u2014 GitHub-specific function with no beads code path\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Teams managing work in beads can run DH agent workflows (grooming, planning, implementation, verification) without creating or maintaining a parallel GitHub Issues mirror\\n- Agent workflows in beads-backend repos operate without network calls to GitHub, eliminating GitHub rate limit failures and authentication overhead during offline or restricted-network sessions\\n- SAM plan creation, task dispatch, and bookend artifact storage work end-to-end using beads primitives (epics, child beads, `bd remember`, molecule epics for wave containers)\\n- The `create_backend()` factory extension registers beads alongside the existing github/sqlite/memory backends \u2014 beads becomes a first-class backend selectable via `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads` or `backend.toml`\\n- The `task_status_hook.py` int cast fix (`parent_issue_number: int \u2192 str | int | None`) resolves a crash path that silently leaves tasks stuck `in-progress` for any non-integer issue ID, benefiting all future backends\\n- Agent and skill instruction files updated for beads compatibility reduce user-visible errors in beads repos; 12 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE files stop attempting GitHub-specific operations that fail silently\\n- The `gate-push` GitHub URL regex (`github.com[:/]`) that crashes on non-GitHub remotes is removed as a failure path\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n**Current behavior:**\\n- Setting `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads` raises `ValueError` (\\\"unknown backend: beads\\\") on the first backlog MCP tool call\\n- `create_artifact_provider(\\\"beads\\\")` raises `BacklogError(\\\"Unknown artifact backend: 'beads'\\\")` unconditionally\\n- `create_task_backend(\\\"beads\\\")` raises `ValueError` (\\\"unknown backend: beads\\\") unconditionally\\n- Any agent running `start-task` in a beads repo that writes a non-integer `parent_issue_number` to active-task context causes `task_status_hook.py` to crash with `ValueError` at line 807, leaving the task stuck `in-progress`\\n\\n**Behavior after this item is complete:**\\n- A repository can set `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads` (or a `.beads/` directory causes auto-detection) and all backlog MCP tool calls succeed against the beads backend without GitHub network calls\\n- `sam_plan create` in a beads-backend repo creates a beads epic; tasks created under it appear as child beads via `--parent`; DAG edges appear via `bd dep add`\\n- `artifact_register` and `artifact_read` store and retrieve artifact manifests in the beads issue metadata JSON blob; artifact content stores in the beads issue notes field\\n- `bd remember` with key `active-task-{session_id}` parks the active task per session; `bd forget` on SubagentStop clears it; no active-task context is lost when MCP session ends\\n- Dispatch wave containers are beads molecule epics; `bd mol bond` tracks membership; `dispatch_stale_check` queries `bd list --parent bd-WAVE`\\n- `task_status_hook.py` handles both integer GitHub issue IDs and non-integer beads IDs without raising; tasks move to COMPLETE state in both backends\\n- The `bd` binary is validated at first use (not at MCP server startup); MCP initialization time is not affected by `bd` availability\\n- Skills `add-new-feature`, `complete-implementation`, `implement-feature`, `start-task`, `work-backlog-item`, `gate-push`, `groom-milestone`, `work-milestone` no longer attempt GitHub-specific operations (PR listing, label management, `github_branches` tool, `#N` issue number parsing) in beads-backend repos\\n- `backlog_update(verified=True)` in a beads repo either maps to the nearest beads equivalent or returns a clear \\\"not supported in beads backend\\\" message rather than silently failing\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads uv run fastmcp call ... backlog_list '{}'` exits 0 and returns a JSON list from the beads backend (not a `ValueError` traceback)\\n2. `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads uv run fastmcp call ... backlog_view '{\\\"selector\\\":\\\"<beads-id>\\\"}'` returns the beads issue body without requiring a GitHub token\\n3. `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads uv run fastmcp call ... artifact_register '{\\\"issue_number\\\":\\\"<beads-id>\\\",\\\"artifact_type\\\":\\\"t0\\\",...}'` exits 0; a subsequent `artifact_read` call returns the same manifest without error\\n4. `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads uv run fastmcp call ... sam_plan '{\\\"config\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"create\\\"},...}'` exits 0 and `bd list` shows a newly created epic\\n5. `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads uv run fastmcp call ... sam_task '{\\\"config\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"claim\\\"},...}'` exits 0 and `bd show <id>` shows the task claimed by the session\\n6. `task_status_hook.py` \u2014 running the hook with a non-integer beads ID in `parent_issue_number` does not raise `ValueError`; the hook exits 0 and the task status transitions to COMPLETE (verify via `bd show <id>` output)\\n7. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_cross_backend.py -k beads` passes with all beads rows in the conformance matrix green\\n8. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_toml_search.py -k beads` passes; `create_backend(\\\"beads\\\")` returns a `BeadsBackend` instance rather than raising `ValueError`\\n9. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py -k beads` passes; `BeadsTaskProvider` satisfies the full `TaskBackend` Protocol\\n10. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_provider_fallback.py -k beads` and `test_artifact_provider_local.py -k beads` pass with `BeadsArtifactProvider` in the test matrix\\n11. MCP server starts in under 5 seconds when `BACKLOG_BACKEND=beads` is set and `bd` binary is absent \u2014 startup does not attempt to validate or install `bd`; only the first actual beads operation triggers the availability check\\n12. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` passes; the agent file no longer hard-codes integer `issue:` field in generated task YAML templates\\n13. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/skills/gate-push/SKILL.md` passes; the `github.com[:/]` regex is removed or made conditional on the backend\\n14. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` passes; the \\\"Primary source of truth is GitHub Issues\\\" statement is qualified by backend\\n15. All 19 INSTRUCTION_UPDATE agent/skill files listed in `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/06-agents-beads-integration.md` and `07-skills-hooks-beads-integration.md` pass `uvx skilllint@latest check` without GitHub-specific tool references in their frontmatter `tools:` lists where those tools have no beads equivalent\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Research report | `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-to-github.html` \u2014 MCP tool mapping (38 tools), SAM system gaps, data model alignment, layer-by-layer impact |\\n| Research file | `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/01-beads-cli-commands.md` \u2014 `bd` CLI command set and `--json` output schemas |\\n| Research file | `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/02-beads-data-model.md` \u2014 beads data model: nanoid IDs, dependency graph, metadata blob, notes field, molecule primitives |\\n| Research file | `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/06-agents-beads-integration.md` \u2014 per-agent evidence for BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE and INSTRUCTION_UPDATE classifications |\\n| Research file | `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/07-skills-hooks-beads-integration.md` \u2014 per-skill evidence for BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE and INSTRUCTION_UPDATE classifications |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` \u2014 `BacklogBackend` Protocol definition and `create_backend()` factory (lines 965\u20131023); `_VALID_BACKENDS` tuple |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` \u2014 `ArtifactBackend` Protocol, `BackendName` StrEnum, `create_artifact_provider()` factory |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 `TaskBackend` Protocol definition |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/context_backend.py` \u2014 `ContextBackend` Protocol; `ActiveTaskContext` field types |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_config.py` \u2014 `create_task_backend()` factory (line 142) |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 prior beads removal comment at lines 107\u2013111 establishing the lazy-validation constraint |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` \u2014 line 807 int cast; type annotation widening needed |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/` \u2014 existing `GitHubBackend`, `SQLiteBackend`, `InMemoryBackend` as implementation patterns |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` \u2014 required reading for backend extension work |\\n| Architecture reference | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 existing beads architecture notes (may be stale) |\\n| RT-ICA result | Stored in backlog item #2279 `## RT-ICA` section \u2014 all 19 conditions AVAILABLE; Decision: APPROVED |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Producer files (must change to enable beads backend):**\\n\\n| File | Change type | Risk |\\n|------|-------------|------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` | Add `\\\"beads\\\"` to `_VALID_BACKENDS`; add beads branch in `create_backend()` | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/artifact_provider.py` | Add `beads = \\\"beads\\\"` to `BackendName` StrEnum; add `BeadsArtifactProvider` branch in `create_artifact_provider()` | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_config.py` | Add `\\\"beads\\\"` to `_VALID_BACKENDS`; return `BeadsTaskProvider` instance in `create_task_backend()` | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py` | New file \u2014 `BeadsBackend` implementing `BacklogBackend` Protocol via `bd --json` subprocess | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/context_backend.py` | Widen `ActiveTaskContext.parent_issue_number` from `int | None` to `str \\\\| int \\\\| None` | MEDIUM |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/__init__.py` | Export `BeadsBackend` if import pattern requires it | LOW |\\n\\n**Consumer files (break under beads IDs without changes):**\\n\\n| File | Change type | Risk |\\n|------|-------------|------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` | Fix `int(data[\\\"parent_issue_number\\\"])` cast at line 807; widen type annotations at lines 417 and 804 | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` | Widen `parent_issue_number` field type in `ActiveTaskContext` storage | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` | Verify no startup hook validates `bd`; preserve prior removal constraint from lines 107\u2013111 | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` | Replace or route around `fetch_tasks_from_github(parent_issue_number: int)` \u2014 GitHub-specific function with no beads code path | HIGH |\\n\\n**Test files (zero beads coverage, require new rows):**\\n\\n| File | Change type | Risk |\\n|------|-------------|------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_cross_backend.py` | Add beads conformance matrix row | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backend_toml_search.py` | Add `create_backend(\\\"beads\\\")` resolution test | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_backend_conformance.py` | Add `BeadsTaskProvider` to Protocol conformance matrix | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_provider_fallback.py` | Add `BeadsArtifactProvider` coverage | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_artifact_provider_local.py` | Add `BeadsArtifactProvider` coverage | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` | Add beads task backend integration path | MEDIUM |\\n\\n**Documentation files (become stale when beads is added):**\\n\\n| File | Change type | Risk |\\n|------|-------------|------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/docs/backend-providers.md` | Add beads entries for both `BacklogBackend` and `TaskBackend` tables | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` | Add `beads` to Backend Providers section valid backend names | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` | Qualify \\\"GitHub Issues as source of truth\\\" statements by backend | MEDIUM |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` | Update `issue` field type documentation from integer-only to `str \\\\| int` | MEDIUM |\\n\\n**Agent/skill instruction files \u2014 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE (12 files):**\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/alignment-analyst.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/plan-validator.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/gate-push/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-milestone/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md`\\n\\n**Agent/skill instruction files \u2014 INSTRUCTION_UPDATE (19 files):** Full list in `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/06-agents-beads-integration.md` and `07-skills-hooks-beads-integration.md`.\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**External prerequisites (must exist in the environment before this item can be verified):**\\n- `bd` CLI binary installed and on `PATH` in the test environment \u2014 required for any end-to-end beads backend test; CI must either provide a `bd` binary or mock subprocess calls via `pytest` patching\\n- beads CLI `--json` output schema stability \u2014 implementation depends on `bd --json` flag producing stable JSON; `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/01-beads-cli-commands.md` documents current schema but upstream changes would require updates\\n\\n**Depends on (backlog items that should be done first):**\\n- None identified \u2014 all 6 architectural decisions are now resolved per RT-ICA (APPROVED 2026-05-14); the BacklogBackend, TaskBackend, ContextBackend, and ArtifactBackend Protocols are confirmed AVAILABLE; the `create_backend()` factory extension pattern is confirmed AVAILABLE\\n\\n**Blocks (items waiting on this one):**\\n- Any backlog item that routes DH workflows in beads-managed repositories\\n- Any item that adds a new DH backend type \u2014 the `parent_issue_number: str | int | None` type widening and `BackendName` StrEnum extension pattern established here must be followed by future backends\\n\\n**Capability gaps (missing beads equivalents noted as MISSING in migration matrix \u2014 require explicit design decisions before those specific sub-tasks can be planned):**\\n- PR listing, label management, GitHub Projects V2, issue comments, and GitHub-only sync have no beads equivalent \u2014 these 5 capability groups are out of scope for this item; callers attempting them in beads repos will receive a \\\"not supported in beads backend\\\" response\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nOverall: XL\\n\\nPhase breakdown by capability layer:\\n\\n| Phase | Capability layer | Effort | Rationale |\\n|-------|-----------------|--------|-----------|\\n| 1 | Backend registration and factory wiring | S | Add `\\\"beads\\\"` to three `_VALID_BACKENDS` tuples, add `beads = \\\"beads\\\"` to `BackendName` StrEnum, wire factory branches in `create_backend()`, `create_artifact_provider()`, `create_task_backend()`. Mechanical \u2014 pattern already established by github/sqlite/memory. |\\n| 2 | `BeadsBackend` implementation (BacklogBackend Protocol) | L | New file implementing all ~38 Protocol methods via `bd --json` subprocess. Each method requires a `bd` CLI invocation, JSON parsing, error handling, and lazy `bd` availability validation. No existing pattern to copy from; must read `01-beads-cli-commands.md` and `02-beads-data-model.md` to map each method. High risk: incomplete implementation leaves all 38 MCP tools broken. |\\n| 3 | SAM task + artifact + context providers | L | Three new provider classes (`BeadsTaskProvider`, `BeadsArtifactProvider`, `BeadsContextBackend`) plus type widening (`parent_issue_number: int \u2192 str \\\\| int \\\\| None`) cascading through `context_backend.py`, `sam_schema/server.py`, `task_status_hook.py:807`, and `implementation_manager.py`. The `task_status_hook.py` fix is independently HIGH risk \u2014 silent `ValueError` leaves tasks stuck. |\\n| 4 | Dispatch and wave state | M | Molecule epic as wave container; `bd mol bond` membership; `dispatch_stale_check` query via `bd list --parent bd-WAVE`. Wave dispatch currently uses SQLite; must validate whether the existing SQLite dispatch state layer is reused or replaced. Architectural decision 5 is resolved; implementation scope is bounded. |\\n| 5 | Test coverage | M | Five test file groups need beads rows: `test_cross_backend.py`, `test_backend_toml_search.py`, `test_task_backend_conformance.py`, `test_artifact_provider_fallback.py`, `test_artifact_provider_local.py`. CI must provide `bd` binary or subprocess mocking. No existing beads fixtures; must be written from scratch. |\\n| 6 | Agent and skill instruction sweep | L | 12 BEHAVIOUR_CHANGE files require content changes (GitHub-specific operations guarded by backend detection or removed); 19 INSTRUCTION_UPDATE files require frontmatter `tools:` list updates and `issue_number` terminology adjustments. Each file must be read, audited against the per-file evidence in `06-agents-beads-integration.md` and `07-skills-hooks-beads-integration.md`, and updated without breaking GitHub-backend behaviour. |\\n\\n**Phases can partially parallelize:** Phase 1 must complete before Phases 2\u20134. Phases 2, 3, and 4 are largely independent once Phase 1 is done. Phase 5 depends on Phases 2\u20134. Phase 6 is independent of Phases 2\u20135 and can run in parallel.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [x] CONTRACT VIOLATION: BdRunner.__init__ missing env_overrides parameter \u2014 verified against bd_runner.py:146. Logged as #2288. (reported by contract-verification on T05)\\n- [x] Pre-implementation alignment analysis \u2014 alignment analyst content describing design-stage concerns (subprocess vs FFI decision, scope expansion, prior beads removal). Not a code-level concern; all questions resolved by the completed implementation. No action required.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n\\n**Rationale**: The decision tree routes this classification because the problem space is not yet bounded. Q1\u2013Q4 all return NO: there is no typo (not procedural), no recurring pattern match (not recurring-pattern), no failing command (not defect), and no missing validation gate (not missing-guardrail). The RT-ICA snapshot confirms the problem space is open \u2014 6 open architectural decisions remain unresolved (plan representation, artifact storage, active-task parking, bookend storage, dispatch/wave state, CLI wrapper scope). The work requires design framing before planning can begin.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: N/A \u2014 unbounded-design does not require root-cause analysis.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Teams using beads for project management must maintain a parallel GitHub Issues mirror to use DH (redundant data entry, network dependency, auth overhead) \u2192 Teams can configure DH to route backlog, task, artifact, and dispatch operations to beads or GitHub based on project backend, and operate without parallel mirrors or network coupling to GitHub during agent workflows.\\n\",\"digest\":\"057f630539f09aef609b5d44a88ac0b756a4334dcf4647e8d8270d3e7233ec57\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCSqDA\"}"}